n     \\]\n\n     The \\(k\\) lines are distinct.  \n     For a fixed \\(j\\) the points of \\(S_k\\) on \\(L_j\\) satisfy  \n\n     \\[\n     a\\ge 1,\\;a+(a+j-t)\\le k+1\\;\\Longrightarrow\\;\n     1\\le a\\le t+1 .\n     \\]\n\n     Hence each \\(L_j\\) contains exactly \\(t+1=\\frac{k+1}{2}=m\\) points of \\(S_k\\), and the \\(k\\) lines are pairwise disjoint.  \n     Translating them by \\((n-k,0)\\) gives \\(k\\) distinct sunny lines covering the whole set \\(T\\).\n\n   *Step 5.4 – the final family.*  \n     The family consisting of the \\(n-k\\) vertical lines of Step 5.1 and the \\(k\\) translated lines of Step 5.3 contains exactly \\(n\\) distinct lines, covers every point of \\(S_n\\), and has precisely \\(k\\) sunny lines.\n\n   This construction works for every \\(k\\) described in the statement, proving sufficiency.\n\n6. **Conclusion.**  \n   The inequality (2) gives the absolute upper bound for the number of sunny lines, while the parity argument shows that only odd values (and \\(0\\)) can be attained. The explicit construction of §5 shows that every admissible value is indeed attainable. Hence the set of all possible numbers \\(k\\) is exactly the one announced in the verdict. ∎\n\n--- \n\n**Answer**\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\;\n\\{0\\}\\ \\cup\\ \\{\\,k\\in\\mathbb Z_{\\ge 1}\\mid k\\text{ odd and }k\\le \n\\begin{cases}\nn      &\\text{if }n\\text{ is odd},\\\\[2mm]\nn-1    &\\text{if }n\\text{ is even}\n\\end{cases}\\}\\;}\n\\]\n\n\n### Verification Task Reminder ###\n\nYour task is to act as an IMO grader. Now, generate the **summary** and the **step-by-step verification log** for the solution above. In your log, justify each correct step and explain in detail any errors or justification gaps you find, as specified in the instructions above.\n\n"
