\n   \\begin{aligned}\n   L_i &: \\; y = x + (2i-2t) \\qquad (i=0,1,\\dots ,t),\\\\[2mm]\n   M_i &: \\; y = -2x + (2t+2+i) \\qquad (i=0,1,\\dots ,t-1).\n   \\end{aligned}\n   \\tag{10}\n   \\]\n\n   *Verification that the lines are sunny.*  \n   The slopes are \\(1\\) (for the \\(L_i\\)) and \\(-2\\) (for the \\(M_i\\)); both are different from \\(0,\\infty,-1\\).\n\n   *Number of points of \\(S_k\\) on each line.*  \n   – For a fixed \\(i\\) the line \\(L_i\\) consists of the points \\((a,b)\\) with \\(b-a=2i-2t\\).  \n     Inside the triangle \\(a+b\\le 2t+2\\) this gives the integer solutions  \n\n     \\[\n     a=1,2,\\dots ,t+1-i,\\qquad b=a+2i-2t .\n     \\]\n\n     Hence \\(|L_i\\cap S_k|=t+1-i\\).\n\n   – For a fixed \\(i\\) the line \\(M_i\\) consists of the points \\((a,b)\\) with \\(b+2a=2t+2+i\\).  \n     The admissible integers are  \n\n     \\[\n     a=1,2,\\dots ,i+1,\\qquad b=2t+2+i-2a .\n     \\]\n\n     Hence \\(|M_i\\cap S_k|=i+1\\).\n\n   Adding the two families we obtain exactly one point for each ordered pair \\((a,b)\\in S_k\\); indeed the numbers\n   \\[\n   (t+1,\\,t,\\,t-1,\\dots ,1)\\quad\\text{and}\\quad(1,2,\\dots ,t)\n   \\]\n   together sum to \\((t+1)+(t)+(t-1)+\\dots +1 = (t+1)^2\\), which is precisely \\(|S_k|=\\frac{(2t+1)(2t+2)}2\\).  Moreover the two families are disjoint because the equations \\(b-a=2i-2t\\) and \\(b+2a=2t+2+j\\) cannot hold simultaneously for the same point with \\(0\\le i\\le t\\) and \\(0\\le j\\le t-1\\).  \n\n   Consequently the \\(k\\) lines in (10) partition \\(S_k\\) and each of them contains exactly \\(t+1=\\frac{k+1}{2}=s_k\\) points.\n\n7. **Putting everything together.**  \n   Let \\(k\\) satisfy (4) and (9).  \n\n   *Step 1.*  Use the vertical lines \\(V_j\\) in (5) for \\(j=1,\\dots ,n-k\\).  They are non‑sunny and together cover all points of \\(S_n\\) with first coordinate \\(\\le n-k\\).\n\n   *Step 2.*  Translate the family \\(\\{L_i,M_i\\}\\) from (10) by the vector \\((n-k,0)\\).  The translation does not change slopes, so the lines remain sunny and stay distinct.  After translation they lie inside the original triangle and cover exactly the remaining points, i.e. the set \\(S_k\\) shifted to the right by \\(n-k\\).\n\n   *Step 3.*  The total number of lines is \\((n-k)+(k)=n\\); exactly \\(k\\) of them (the translated \\(L_i,M_i\\)) are sunny, and every point of \\(S_n\\) lies on at least one of the lines.\n\n   Hence for every integer \\(k\\) that fulfills (4) and (9) a configuration exists.\n\n8. **Conclusion.**  \n   The necessary conditions derived from the counting arguments (4) and the parity condition (9) are also sufficient, thanks to the explicit construction above.  Therefore the set of all admissible values of \\(k\\) is exactly the one stated in the boxed answer.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\; \\{0\\}\\ \\cup\\ \\Bigl\\{\\,k\\in\\mathbb Z_{\\ge 1}\\;:\\;\nk\\text{ odd and } \nk\\le \n\\begin{cases}\nn      &\\text{if }n\\text{ is odd},\\\\[2mm]\nn-1    &\\text{if }n\\text{ is even}\n\\end{cases}\n\\Bigr\\}\\;}\n\\]"
